# Keep the build context to the sources `docker/Dockerfile` actually publishes.
#
# Without this file the context is whatever the working tree happens to hold: on a developer
# machine that includes src/**/bin, src/**/obj and build_out/, which is ~800 MB and made local
# `docker build` runs fail on context transfer. CI never noticed because a fresh checkout has
# none of it. Local builds are how this Docker-only product gets verified before release, so
# they have to work.
#
# Everything not listed here is still copied: the Dockerfile does `COPY . .` and then publishes
# src/GroupDocs.Search.Mcp/GroupDocs.Search.Mcp.csproj, so src/, build/ and any root-level
# MSBuild or NuGet settings must stay in.

# Build output
**/bin/
**/obj/
build_out/
TestResults/

# Version control and CI
.git/
.github/
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# Editor / IDE state
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user

# Docs and release material: not compiled, and they change on almost every commit,
# which would otherwise bust the build cache for no reason.
*.md
docs/
changelog/
assets/
install/

# The image never builds itself
docker/
.dockerignore
